{
  "id": "c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia",
  "level": "C1",
  "version": 1,
  "topic": "Memory and nostalgia",
  "parts": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Interview",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p1-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Good evening. First of all, we'd like to know a little about you.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p1-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q1",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, what are your earliest memories?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p1-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q2",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, do you enjoy looking back at the past?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p1-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3900
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q3",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, is there anything from your childhood you miss?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p1-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q4",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, why do you think some people tend to say that the past was better?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p1-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Long turn",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p2-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "In this part of the test, I'm going to give each of you three pictures. I'd like you to talk about two of them on your own for about a minute, and also to answer a question briefly about your partner's pictures.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p2-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13200
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e29-a1",
            "c1-e29-a2",
            "c1-e29-a3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate A, your pictures show people remembering the past. Choose two of the pictures and say what feelings the people might have, and why these memories might be important to them.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p2-a.mp3",
          "audioMs": 12000
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate B, do you enjoy looking at old photographs or objects?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p2-a-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4900
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e29-b1",
            "c1-e29-b2",
            "c1-e29-b3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate B, your pictures show people connected with the past. Choose two of the pictures and say why it might be important to remember the past, and how different people might do this.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p2-b.mp3",
          "audioMs": 12100
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate A, how should a society remember its history?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p2-b-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Collaborative task",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p3-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like you to talk about something together for about two minutes. Here are some ways of keeping memories alive, and a question for you to discuss.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p3-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 9600
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-discuss",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 120,
          "diagram": "c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia",
          "text": "Talk to each other about this question: How might these ways of preserving memories help future generations?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p3-discuss.mp3",
          "audioMs": 7800
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-decide",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "diagram": "c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia",
          "text": "Now you have about a minute to decide together. Which is the most valuable?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p3-decide.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p4-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like to ask you some more questions about memory and nostalgia.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p4-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5300
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q1",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Does nostalgia help us or does it hold us back?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p4-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q2",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, to what extent can digital photographs and social media replace traditional ways of remembering?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p4-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 8200
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q3",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, do you think it is always healthy to dwell on the past?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p4-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4900
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q4",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Why is it important for societies to remember difficult periods in their history?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p4-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6000
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q5",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, how reliable are personal memories as a record of the past?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p4-q5.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q6",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, should old objects and buildings always be kept for their emotional value?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e29-memory-and-nostalgia/p4-q6.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6300
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
